      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, i think. the sentiment is definitely there, but it feels a bit... safe? like, maybe a little too plain. \n\ni just ran it through the analytics tool we talked about to see where we stand, and the \"inspiration metric\" came back really low. it's flagging the draft as \"emotionally thin\" or \"dry.\" i know i said not to go overboard, but the candidate really needs that emotional punch to rally the crowd. \n\ncan we try another version? maybe go a bit deeper into the passion and the vision? try to bump up that density a bit so it actually registers as inspiring on the metric, but please, just keep it grounded. i really don't want it to look like you're just trying to cheat the score, it just needs more weight.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
